---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Give a member another role.

Usage: ink org member role [OPTIONS] <ORG> <ACCOUNT> <ROLE>

Examples
  # Make a member an admin
  ink org member role 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210 admin

Arguments
  <ORG>      The organization's id
  <ACCOUNT>  The person's account id
  <ROLE>     What they may do from now on: owner, admin,
             writer or reader

Account
      --api <URL>
        The API's address, `http://host[:port]`;
        `account.api` in the config file [env: INK_API]
      --timeout <SECONDS>
        Seconds one call may take [default: 30]
        [env: INK_TIMEOUT]

Notes
  An organization's last owner cannot be given a lower role
  or removed.

Exit codes
  0  Done
  2  Wrong usage: no API named, a key that is none, a
     private key that would print to a terminal
  3  No key, or the API refused the signature, or nobody
     approved the key in time
  4  The API could not be reached or failed; safe to retry

Environment
  INK_API       The address of the API, as --api
  INK_SITE      The site's id, as --site
  INK_KEY       The private key to sign requests with, for a
                CI job; never a flag, so it stays out of
                process lists. `ink login` keeps one in the
                config folder instead
  INK_KEY_FILE  A file that holds that key, in place of
                INK_KEY

Docs    https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global  -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log,
        --log-file (see `ink --help`)
